    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDespite https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41725 not being the right solution, being able to hook into watchers and provide your own custom refresh behavior is a very nice primitive to have. Note that dealing with watchers is NOT trivial (lifecycle, shutdown, deduping, etc.), so the \"just write a recipe, bro\" approach is not ideal.\n\nFor example, vim-fugitive could use a watcher on the git directory and refresh its rendered view of changes accordingly.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSome API to provide custom refresh logic (that is NOT the approach in #41725).",
